A can complete a piece of work in 15 days, and B can complete the same work in 20 days. They work together for 5 days. What fraction of the work is still remaining?

A) \(\frac{1}{4}\)
B) \(\frac{5}{12}\)
C) \(\frac{7}{12}\)
D) \(\frac{2}{3}\)

Answer: B) \(\frac{5}{12}\)

Explanation:

A's 1-day work:

$$ \frac{1}{15} $$

B's 1-day work:

$$ \frac{1}{20} $$

Together:

$$ \frac{1}{15}+\frac{1}{20} =\frac{4+3}{60} =\frac{7}{60} $$

In 5 days:

$$ 5\times\frac{7}{60}=\frac{35}{60}=\frac{7}{12} $$

So, work completed:

$$ \frac{7}{12} $$

Work remaining:

$$ 1-\frac{7}{12}=\boxed{\frac{5}{12}} $$

✅ Answer: B) 
